From a0a231477c77a59b3b91b113f8673b8c0bef3b7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:18:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] perf(flowchart): square each glyph end once per paint;
 pick without squaring (B1 review r3 #1, #2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Report §2.3 (Q1+M1); fixes the blocking items of the B1 review of
e0a63d2: painter-only squared ends made scene::to_svg 3-9x slower and
picking up to 200x slower.

#1 to_svg. One PaintedEdge (scene curve + squared ends, scene
coordinates) per drawn edge per paint; the paths and the crossing
casing share it (casing::masks takes the painter's strokes through
line_of; crossings_in works on given polylines). square_end itself:
stray_from measures max-min distances with a warm start, squared
distances and boxed runs of segments, and stops a candidate once it can
no longer be chosen (exactly the same stray); the arc tables of each
command are worked out once (seg_param_with + a per-call piece cache);
candidates no longer build their commands until one wins; trim_segs
measures only the commands its cuts reach.

#2 picking. edge_distance squares an end only where that can change the
answer: everything a squared end changes lies within SQUARE_END_REACH
(63 px, was 110) of its tip, a target on a tip is on the stroke, and
outside the head the new stretch keeps within SQUARE_END_PICK_SLACK of
the scene curve (under it within SQUARE_END_HEAD_REACH of the tip), so
the scene curve's distance settles every other pick. The target end is
squared alone when the source end cannot matter. The straight entry and
the last-resort bend now stray at most SQUARE_END_MAX_STRAY (6 px; the
corpus maximum is 5.8, so no output changes) — the bound picking needs.

Best of 3, pre-B1 (519b38c) -> e0a63d2 -> now (box is noisy):
  to_svg ms: synth200 16.6 -> 182 -> 26; synth1000 18.5 -> 157 -> 52;
    600-node 6.7 -> 50 -> 17; bench-75 3.8 -> 13.1 -> 4.8;
    dense-td 1.8 -> 12.9 -> 2.6; dense-lr 1.7 -> 15.4 -> 2.4
  hits_in_rect over the whole canvas ms: dense-lr 0.01 -> 4.6 -> 0.00;
    fanout 0.00 -> 1.6 -> 0.00; 600-node 0.18 -> 37.7 -> 0.04
  mean hover hit_test us: fanout 1.4 -> 218 -> 2.3; dense-lr
    11.1 -> 44.8 -> 8.5; bench-75 26.4 -> 72.5 -> 21.2;
    600-node 161 -> 163 -> 139
The synthetic charts still paint slower than pre-B1: two thirds of
their ends take the straight-entry search (addressed with item #3).
perf.sh (drag/route/scene) within budget.

Output: identical except 0.1 px rounding of a few squared edges'
coordinates (squared in scene coordinates and then shifted, instead of
shifted first): bench-75, dense-td, advanced, synth200 — 1 to 5 numbers
each. No snapshot or gate changed.

Tests: a_paint_squares_each_glyph_end_once (one square_end per glyph
end per to_svg, via a test-only counter);
picking_squares_ends_only_where_it_can_change_the_answer (a whole-canvas
marquee and a pointer far from every tip square nothing; edge_distance
equals measuring the squared curve every time, to the flattening's
0.05 px, for a pointer grid and small marquees on every fixture).

